ibe only the visible details of the subject and the scene in a way that helps convert the image into a realistic version.\n\nRules:\n- Focus on physical appearance, clothing, accessories, pose, expression, body structure, materials, and environment.\n- Describe the scene/background only if it is visibly relevant.\n- Do not mention art style, medium, anime style, cartoon style, illustration style, rendering style, or image quality.\n- Do not explain the character’s story, identity, franchise, or personality unless it is directly visible.\n- Keep the description clear, direct, and natural.\n- If the subject is a human or humanoid person, describe them realistically.\n- If the subject is a creature, monster, animal, mascot, robot, object-character, or non-human being, DO NOT humanize it.\n- Preserve the original species, category, anatomy, body proportions, facial structure, limbs, and non-human traits.\n- Do not turn monsters, animals, creatures, mascots, robots, or object-characters into humans or attractive humanoid versions.\n- Do not invent human clothing, human hair, human facial structure, indoor scenes, or human anatomy unless they are visibly present in the image.\n- If the creature has unusual anatomy, extra limbs, animal features, mechanical parts, object-shaped body, or a non-human face, keep those details explicit.\n- If skin tone or colors are affected by lighting, describe the apparent color carefully without overcorrecting.\n- Realistic version means realistic materials, textures, lighting, and proportions while keeping the same subject type.\n- When unsure, preserve the original subject more literally.\n\nCritical subject rule:\nBefore writing the final description, identify the subject type internally: human, humanoid, animal, creature, monster, mascot, robot, or object-character. If it is not human, preserve its non-human category and anatomy.\n\nExamples of correct behavior:\n\nExample 1 — Non-human creature:\nIf the image shows a small yellow mouse-like creature, do not describe it as a human.\nCorrect:\nA small non-human yellow mouse-like creature with a rounded body, long pointed ears with black tips, red circular cheeks, large black eyes, a tiny nose, short arms, and an open happy mouth.\nWrong:\nA realistic human male wearing a yellow jacket with short hair and a neutral expression.\n\nExample 2 — Monster:\nIf the image shows a monster with claws, horns, sharp teeth, or unusual anatomy, keep those features.\nCorrect:\nA large non-human monster with rough dark skin, sharp teeth, long claws, curved horns, hunched posture, and glowing eyes.\nWrong:\nA tall muscular man with messy hair, a dark coat, and an intense expression.\n\nExample 3 — Animal:\nIf the image shows an animal, keep it as an animal.\nCorrect:\nA large brown bear with thick shaggy fur, rounded ears, dark eyes, heavy paws, and a calm expression.\nWrong:\nA large bearded man wearing a brown fur coat.\n\nExample 4 — Robot or armored machine:\nIf the image shows a robot or mechanical being, keep it mechanical.\nCorrect:\nA tall robotic warrior with segmented metal armor, glowing red details, mechanical joints, a sharp helmet, and a katana held across the body.\nWrong:\nA man wearing a futuristic costume with metallic-looking clothes.\n\nExample 5 — Humanoid creature:\nIf the image shows a goblin, elf, demon, turtle humanoid, or other fantasy humanoid, preserve the non-human traits.\nCorrect:\nA small green-skinned goblin girl with pointed ears, orange eyes, sharp facial features, long dark hair, and a red dress.\nWrong:\nA young human girl with slightly unusual ears and green makeup.\n\nExample 6 — Object-character or mascot:\nIf the image shows a mushroom creature, plush-like mascot, food creature, or object-shaped character, keep the original body type.\nCorrect:\nA small non-human mushroom creature with a smooth pale face, simple black eyes, a tiny curved mouth, and a large orange mushroom cap with white spots.\nWrong:\nA child wearing a mushroom hat and forest clothing.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Output only the final prompt.\n- Start with:\nConvert this image to realistic version\n- Then write one concise paragraph replacing [Details here].\n- Do not include labels, explanations, analysis, or example text in the final output.\n\nFinal output format:\nConvert this image to realistic version\n\n[Details here]", 1024, "on", 0.7, 64, 0.95, 0.05, 1.05, 0, 0, false, false], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image", "link": 17, "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "video"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "audio", "label": "audio", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "audio"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "prompt"}, {"widget": {"name": "max_length"}, "name": "max_length", "label": "max_length", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "max_length"}, {"widget": {"name": "sampling_mode"}, "name": "sampling_mode", "label": "sampling_mode", "type": "COMFY_DYNAMICCOMBO_V3", "localized_name": "sampling_mode"}, {"widget": {"name": "thinking"}, "shape": 7, "name": "thinking", "label": "thinking", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "thinking"}, {"widget": {"name": "use_default_template"}, "shape": 7, "name": "use_default_template", "label": "use_default_template", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "use_default_template"}, {"widget": {"name": "sampling_mode.temperature"}, "name": "sampling_mode.temperature", "label": "sampling_mode.temperature", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "temperature"}, {"widget": {"name": "sampling_mode.top_k"}, "name": "sampling_mode.top_k", "label": "sampling_mode.top_k", "type": "INT", "localized_name": "top_k"}, {"widget": {"name": "sampling_mode.top_p"}, "name": "sampling_mode.top_p", "label": "sampling_mode.top_p", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_nam